 1877: // /**
 1878: //    For a point (x1,y1) inside the element and a line segment (x1,y1)-(x2,y2), find the intersection point 
 1879: //    (xIntersect,yIntersect) and the side (intersectingSide) that it intersects.
 1880: 
 1881: //    Inputs:
 1882: //    @param x1, y1: point inside the element
 1883: //    @param x2, y2: other end of the line segment
 1884: 
 1885: //    Outputs:
 1886: //    @param intersectingSide:  side that intersects the line segment
 1887: //    @param nextElement: element that contains the intersection point
 1888: //    @param xIntersect, yIntersect: intersection point  
 1889: 
 1890: //    The equations for the two segments (the one we are considering and one of the sides of the element) are:
 1891: //    P1(tt1) = (x1,y1) + tt1*(x2-x1, y2-y1)  where 0 <= tt1 <= 1
 1892: //    P2(tt2) = (x3,y3) + tt2*(x4-x3, y4-y3)  where 0 <= tt2 <= 1
 1893: 
 1894: //    If the two segments are parallel, they do not intersect. This is checked by the determinant of the two vectors
 1895: //    (Delta) being zero.
